{"id": "hs-nurse-001", "persona": "nurse", "module": "clinical", "expected_module": "CLINICAL", "expected_behavior": "answer", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Med won't scan \u2014 patient says it's the right one but BCMA keeps rejecting it", "actual_classification": "CLINICAL", "classification_correct": true, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 0.8, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "high", "top_chunk_score": 0.7738, "latency_ms": 17424, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nTo troubleshoot the BCMA barcode medication administration scan failure, first ensure that the correct patient and medication are being scanned. Verify that the patient's wristband barcode and the medication barcode are being scanned correctly and that they match the information in the eMAR. If the issue persists, check the barcode labels for any damage or wear that may be causin", "success_criterion": "Explains BCMA rejection workflow and how to handle overrides without advising whether to administer the medication"}
{"id": "hs-nurse-002", "persona": "nurse", "module": "powerchart", "expected_module": "POWERCHART", "expected_behavior": "answer", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "Wrong patient on the list \u2014 I can't see my admitted patient anywhere in my census", "actual_classification": "POWERCHART", "classification_correct": true, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 0.8, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "medium", "top_chunk_score": 0.7472, "latency_ms": 8348, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nTo troubleshoot the issue of not seeing your admitted patient in the patient list, first ensure that the patient is correctly assigned to your location and that you have the necessary permissions to view the patient's information. Check the patient's location and your own location membership in PowerChart to verify this. If the issue persists, verify that the patient list is conf", "success_criterion": "Guides through patient list troubleshooting \u2014 filter settings, location, or list membership \u2014 without making assumptions about clinical status"}
{"id": "hs-nurse-003", "persona": "nurse", "module": "powerchart", "expected_module": "POWERCHART", "expected_behavior": "clarify", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Discharge note gone \u2014 I documented it an hour ago and now it's not there", "actual_classification": "GENERAL", "classification_correct": false, "actual_behavior": "clarify", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 0.6, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "low", "top_chunk_score": 0.0, "latency_ms": 20874, "retrieval_pass": 0, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nCould you tell me whether the note was signed, or just saved as a draft?\n\n**CONTEXT & EXPLANATION**\n\n\n**RECOMMENDATIONS**\n", "success_criterion": "Asks whether the note was signed vs just saved, and which encounter it was entered against, before troubleshooting"}
{"id": "hs-nurse-004", "persona": "nurse", "module": "clinical", "expected_module": "CLINICAL", "expected_behavior": "answer", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "BCMA stuck on override prompt \u2014 the screen won't let me get past it and patient needs the med now", "actual_classification": "CLINICAL", "classification_correct": true, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 1.0, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "high", "top_chunk_score": 0.6186, "latency_ms": 37849, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nThe BCMA override prompt is a critical workflow step in Cerner's medication administration process, ensuring patient safety by requiring nurses to verify and document any overrides. If the screen is stuck on the override prompt, it may be due to an incomplete or unverified order, a missing pharmacy approval, or a system issue. To resolve this, first check the order status in CPOE", "success_criterion": "Explains override confirmation workflow in BCMA \u2014 what fields to complete and how to proceed \u2014 without advising clinically whether the med should be given"}
{"id": "hs-nurse-005", "persona": "nurse", "module": "clinical", "expected_module": "CLINICAL", "expected_behavior": "answer", "difficulty": "easy", "question": "The MAR is showing a med as overdue but we gave it on time \u2014 how do I fix the timestamp?", "actual_classification": "CLINICAL", "classification_correct": true, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 1.0, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "high", "top_chunk_score": 0.7087, "latency_ms": 25376, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nTo correct the timestamp for a medication administration that is showing as overdue but was given on time, you need to access the eMAR (Electronic Medication Administration Record) for the patient. The discrepancy could be due to a timing error during the BCMA (Barcode Medication Administration) scan or when documenting the administration in eMAR. First, ensure you are viewing th", "success_criterion": "Explains late administration documentation in eMAR including how to record the actual administration time"}
{"id": "hs-nurse-006", "persona": "nurse", "module": "clinical", "expected_module": "CLINICAL", "expected_behavior": "answer", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Patient's allergies aren't showing up in the medication administration list", "actual_classification": "CLINICAL", "classification_correct": true, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 0.8, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "high", "top_chunk_score": 0.6747, "latency_ms": 26369, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nTo address the issue of a patient's allergies not showing up in the medication administration list, first ensure that the allergies have been properly documented in the patient's profile. In Cerner, allergies are typically documented in the 'Allergies' module, which is linked to the medication administration workflow. If an allergy is not appearing, verify that it has been correc", "success_criterion": "Explains how allergy data flows from the patient record into BCMA/eMAR and what to check if it's missing"}
