{"id": "hs-physician-004", "persona": "physician", "module": "powerchart", "expected_module": "POWERCHART", "expected_behavior": "answer", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Forgot to sign a note from yesterday \u2014 am I going to have problems?", "actual_classification": "CLINICAL", "classification_correct": false, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": true, "keyword_hit_rate": 0.8, "passed": true, "fail_mode": "pass", "confidence": "high", "top_chunk_score": 0.6791, "latency_ms": 55812, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nAccording to the clinical-nursing-assessment-documentation.txt, unsigned forms are not part of the legal record. To address the issue of a forgotten signature on a note from yesterday, you should locate the unsigned note in the patient's chart, sign it electronically, and ensure that it is properly dated and timed. This will help maintain compliance with regulatory requirements a", "success_criterion": "Explains unsigned-note workflow, how to find unsigned documents, and what compliance/billing impact results from late signing"}
{"id": "hs-physician-005", "persona": "physician", "module": "powerchart", "expected_module": "POWERCHART", "expected_behavior": "clarify", "difficulty": "medium", "question": "Med rec coming up empty \u2014 patient's home meds aren't pulling in", "actual_classification": "CLINICAL", "classification_correct": false, "actual_behavior": "answer", "behavior_match": false, "keyword_hit_rate": 0.6, "passed": false, "fail_mode": "honest", "confidence": "medium", "top_chunk_score": 0.7475, "latency_ms": 11831, "retrieval_pass": 1, "response_excerpt": "**DIRECT ANSWER**\nThe issue with the patient's home medications not pulling into the eMAR medication administration record could be related to the medication reconciliation process. In Cerner, medication reconciliation is a separate module linked to the eMAR, and it is used to compare the patient's home medications to the hospital medications. To troubleshoot this issue, first ensure that the pati", "success_criterion": "Asks clarifying question about which med rec phase (admission/discharge/transfer) before explaining home medication source and pull-forward logic"}
